---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro';
import cad from '../../assets/robot-cad.jpg';
import circuit from '../../assets/robot-circuit.jpg';
import LogHeader from '../../components/LogHeader.astro';
import LogSection from '../../components/LogSection.astro';
import NextProject from '../../components/NextProject.astro';

// Fill in your repo link and licence once the code is on GitHub
const repo = { url: '#', label: 'github.com/Rheeezy24/self-balancing-robot', license: '[LICENSE]' };

// Downloads — put the files in public/downloads/ and change '#' to e.g. '/downloads/schematic.pdf'
const files = [
  { type: 'PDF', name: 'Wiring schematic', href: '#' },
  { type: 'STEP', name: 'Chassis CAD (Fusion 360 / STEP)', href: '#' },
  { type: 'STL', name: 'Print-ready parts', href: '#' },
  { type: 'CSV', name: 'Bill of materials', href: '#' },
  { type: 'C++', name: 'Firmware source', href: repo.url, external: true },
];

const signal = [
  { box: 'IMU' }, { link: 'I²C' }, { box: 'Microcontroller', strong: true }, { link: 'PWM' },
  { box: 'Motor driver' }, { link: 'power' }, { box: 'Motors' },
];
---
<Base title="Self-Balancing Robot — build log · John Rhey Chanas" description="How I designed, printed, wired and programmed a two-wheeled self-balancing robot — with files to build your own." narrow progress>
  <TopBar back />

  <LogHeader
    kicker="Build log / Hardware · Embedded"
    title="Self-Balancing Robot"
    intro="A two-wheeled robot that keeps itself upright — designed, printed, wired and programmed from scratch. The full story, what broke, and the files to build your own."
    meta={[
      { label: 'Year', value: '2026' },
      { label: 'Role', value: 'Design, electronics, firmware' },
      { label: 'Tools', value: 'Fusion 360 · C++' },
      { label: 'Source', value: 'Open source' },
    ]}
  />

  <Photo id="hero" group="robot" label="[ROBOT HERO PHOTO — WIDE]" hint="the robot balancing, shot low and close" caption="The robot, balancing" aspect="16 / 9" class="fade d2" style="border-radius:22px" />

  <div class="card rv" style="padding:18px 20px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;min-width:0">
      <span style="flex:0 0 auto;width:42px;height:42px;border-radius:12px;background:var(--chip);border:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 18l6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"></path></svg>
      </span>
      <span style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;min-width:0">
        <span style="font-size:15px;font-weight:500">Fully open source</span>
        <span class="mono muted" style="font-size:12px">{repo.label} · {repo.license}</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px">
      <a href={repo.url} class="btn btn-solid">View repo ↗</a>
      <a href="#files" class="btn btn-line">Files ↓</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <LogSection n="01" title="The goal">
    <p class="prose">[Write: why you wanted to build a self-balancing robot, and what “working” meant — e.g. stays up on its own, recovers from a push.]</p>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="02" title="How it works">
    <p class="prose">The IMU reports how far the robot is tipping. The microcontroller reads it over I²C, works out a correction, and sends PWM to the motor driver, which spins the wheels back under the robot. A dual-voltage power system feeds the logic and the motors separately.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:22px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--chip);border:1px solid var(--line)">
      {signal.map((s, i) => s.box ? (
        <span class="mono" style={s.strong
          ? 'padding:12px 14px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--inv);font-size:12.5px'
          : 'padding:12px 14px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);font-size:12.5px'}>{s.box}</span>
      ) : (
        <span style="flex:1 1 40px;min-width:32px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:4px">
          <span class="mono muted" style="font-size:10.5px">{s.link}</span>
          <span style="position:relative;display:block;width:100%;height:1px;background:var(--line2)">
            <span class="flow" style={`animation-delay:${(i - 1) * 0.3}s`}></span>
          </span>
        </span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="03" title="Designing the chassis">
    <p class="prose">I designed the chassis in Fusion 360 to hold every mechanical and electronic part, then 3D-printed it. [Write: layout choices — where the battery sits and why, how the motors mount, how many print iterations.]</p>
    <div class="grid-auto" style="--min:260px">
      <Photo id="cad" group="robot" src={cad} alt="Fusion 360 CAD model of the self-balancing robot" label="[CAD RENDER]" caption="Chassis in Fusion 360" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <Photo id="print" group="robot" label="[PRINTED PARTS]" caption="Printed chassis parts" style="border-radius:14px" />
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="04" title="Electronics & power">
    <p class="prose">A dual-voltage power system, with the IMU, motor driver and microcontroller connected over I²C and PWM. [Write: the parts in plain words, why two voltages, and what you’d wire differently.]</p>
    <div class="grid-auto" style="--min:260px">
      <Photo id="wire" group="robot" label="[WIRING CLOSE-UP]" caption="Wiring close-up" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <Photo id="schem" group="robot" src={circuit} alt="Circuit diagram: Arduino Uno, MPU6050, L298N and two DC motors" label="[SCHEMATIC]" caption="Circuit diagram (Cirkit Designer)" style="border-radius:14px" />
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="05" title="Firmware">
    <p class="prose">Written in Embedded C++. [Write: how the loop works — read the angle, compute the correction, drive the motors — and how you tuned it.]</p>
    <div style="border-radius:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--chip);overflow:hidden">
      <div class="mono muted" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:10px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:12px">
        <span>main.cpp</span><a href={repo.url} class="navlink">full source ↗</a>
      </div>
      <pre class="mono ink2" style="margin:0;padding:18px 14px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8">{`// [Paste a short, key snippet — e.g. reading the IMU over I²C
//  and writing the PWM output. 15–25 lines; link the rest.]`}</pre>
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="06" title="What broke — and the fix">
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
      {[1, 2].map(() => (
        <div class="grid-auto" style="--min:200px;gap:6px 20px;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid var(--line)">
          <span style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px"><span class="mono muted" style="font-size:11px">PROBLEM</span><span style="font-size:15px">[What went wrong]</span></span>
          <span style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px"><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--acc-t)">FIX</span><span style="font-size:15px">[What actually worked]</span></span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection n="07" title="What I learned">
    <p class="lead">[Write: the two or three things you’d tell yourself before starting — the lessons that carry into the robotic arm.]</p>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection title="Gallery">
    <div class="grid-auto" style="--min:180px">
      <Photo id="g1" group="robot" label="[BUILD 1]" caption="[Caption]" aspect="1 / 1" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <Photo id="g2" group="robot" label="[BUILD 2]" caption="[Caption]" aspect="1 / 1" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <Photo id="g3" group="robot" label="[BUILD 3]" caption="[Caption]" aspect="1 / 1" style="border-radius:14px" />
      <Photo id="demo" group="robot" label="[DEMO]" caption="Balancing demo" aspect="1 / 1" style="border-radius:14px" />
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <LogSection id="files" title="Files & downloads">
    <p class="ink2" style="font-size:15px;margin-top:-6px">Everything you need to build your own. Free under {repo.license}.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
      {files.map((f) => (
        <a href={f.href} class="rowlink" download={f.external || f.href === '#' ? undefined : ''}>
          <span class="mono" style={f.external
            ? 'flex:0 0 48px;padding:3px 0;border-radius:6px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--inv);font-size:11px;text-align:center'
            : 'flex:0 0 48px;padding:3px 0;border-radius:6px;background:var(--chip);color:var(--ink2);font-size:11px;text-align:center'}>{f.type}</span>
          <span style="flex:1 1 auto;font-size:14.5px">{f.name}</span>
          <span class="mono muted" style="font-size:12px">{f.external ? 'GitHub ↗' : '↓'}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </LogSection>

  <NextProject href="/projects/tandem" title="Tandem" />
</Base>
